  "problem": "Which of the following pairs of sets are disjoint?\n\n- ${2,4,8}$ and ${8,16,32}$\n- ${1,e,\\pi }$ and ${0,1,2}$\n- $(-\\infty ,0)$ and $(0,\\infty )$",
  "worked_solution": "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=\u2205\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Pair I is *not* disjoint since the intersection of the sets is not empty:\n\n$$\n{2,4,8}\\cap {8,16,32}={8}\\ne \u2205\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- Pair II is *not* disjoint since the intersection of the sets is not empty:\n\n$$\n{1,e,\\pi }\\cap {0,1,2}={1}\\ne \u2205\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\n- Pair III is disjoint. Indeed, the intersection of the sets is empty:\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,0)\\cap (0,\\infty )=\u2205\\,\\,\u2713\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
